# Attacks from ring 2 (roadmap l4.md L7, The attacks): the program in ring
# 2, which asked for IOPL as a driver would and got 0 (only ring 1 gets
# it); then IN, OUT, CLI, the kernel's data, and binding the timer's line,
# for which no capability exists. tests/programs/rings.asm.
program: rings
define: TEST_RING2
---
rx286, test build
rings: IOPL
rings: its IOPL: 0
rings: in
rx286: program fault #GP(0000) at 0006:{attacks.in}
rings: out
rx286: program fault #GP(0000) at 0006:{attacks.out}
rings: cli
rx286: program fault #GP(0000) at 0006:{attacks.cli}
rings: kernel data
rx286: program fault #GP(0010) at 0006:{attacks.kdata.load}
rings: bind the timer's line
rings: refused, status 1
rings: done
